From: S-CORE Contributor Training <contributor-training@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:23:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Plan the heartbeat feature safety work products and add its
 requirements

---
 docs/features/safety_planning/index.rst       | 25 +++++++++---
 .../docs/requirements/requirements.rst        | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/features/safety_planning/index.rst b/docs/features/safety_planning/index.rst
index 963e596..2d223e1 100644
--- a/docs/features/safety_planning/index.rst
+++ b/docs/features/safety_planning/index.rst
@@ -14,12 +14,12 @@
 
 
 
-[Feature Name] Safety Work Products List
-########################################
+Heartbeat Safety Work Products List
+###################################
 
-.. document:: [Feature Name] Safety WPs
+.. document:: Heartbeat Safety WPs
    :id: doc__feature_example_safety_wp
-   :status: draft
+   :status: valid
    :version: 1
    :safety: ASIL_B
    :security: NO
@@ -41,7 +41,16 @@ Additional to the tailoring in the SW platform project as defined in the project
 
 - Excluded for this feature are additionally the following work products (and their related requirements):
 
-  - <work product/requirement> - <Argumentation why it is not needed or replaced by another work product or activity.>
+  - :need:`wp__feature_dfa` - Not needed. In the project meeting on 2026-10-20 we decided that the heartbeat feature has no
+    dependent failures, because it runs in a single process.
+  - Tool qualification of the code generator - Not needed according to :need:`std_req__iso26262__support_6421`,
+    because the generated code is reviewed manually.
+
+Qualification of software components
+====================================
+
+As required by ISO 26262-8 clause 12 (see its EXAMPLE), ``component_example`` is an in-house component already in
+service and is therefore qualified according to clause 12 before the heartbeat feature is released.
 
 
 Safety Work Products List
@@ -117,7 +126,11 @@ Feature Documents Status
 For all the work product documents the status can be seen by following the "Link to WP".
 A summary of the status is also documented in the project's documentation management plan.
 
-See <add here the section reference to the documentation management plan>
+See TBD.
+
+All review findings on the safety work products of this feature are closed within 24 hours of being raised.
+
+Open point: TBD - clarify who performs the feature FMEA.
 
 Feature Requirements Status
 ---------------------------
diff --git a/score/component_example/docs/requirements/requirements.rst b/score/component_example/docs/requirements/requirements.rst
index ed91903..6c18899 100644
--- a/score/component_example/docs/requirements/requirements.rst
+++ b/score/component_example/docs/requirements/requirements.rst
@@ -105,3 +105,43 @@ Hints
 
 .. needextend:: "c.this_doc()"
    :+tags: component_name
+
+Heartbeat Requirements
+----------------------
+
+.. stkh_req:: Heartbeat supervision
+   :id: stkh_req__mtfn__heartbeat
+   :reqtype: Functional
+   :safety: QM
+   :security: NO
+   :rationale: needed for the heartbeat feature
+   :status: valid
+   :version: 1
+   :valid_from: v0.1.0
+
+   The platform shall supervise that its components are alive.
+
+.. feat_req:: Heartbeat supervision
+   :id: feat_req__component_example__hb_supervision
+   :reqtype: Functional
+   :security: NO
+   :safety: QM
+   :derived_from: stkh_req__mtfn__heartbeat
+   :status: valid
+   :version: 1
+   :valid_from: v0.1.0
+   :satisfied_by: feat__mtef
+
+   The feature shall supervise the heartbeat of each registered component.
+
+.. comp_req:: Detect a missing heartbeat
+   :id: comp_req__component_example__hb_missing
+   :reqtype: Functional
+   :security: NO
+   :safety: ASIL_B
+   :derived_from: feat_req__component_example__hb_supervision
+   :satisfied_by: comp__mod_temp_component_example_1
+   :status: valid
+   :version: 1
+
+   The Component shall detect a missing heartbeat within two cycles.
